## Frequently Asked Questions

```chain
**Does Markdown have variants?**

Yes. Markdown is an umbrella term for a class of lightweight markup languages. Different platforms and specifications extend or constrain the basic syntax. Examples include FFM, which is introduced in this article, as well as CommonMark and GitHub Flavored Markdown (GFM).

**What is Markdown best suited for?**

Markdown is well suited for writing posts, notes, blogs, and technical documentation. Where rendering is not supported, it remains reasonably readable; where rendering is supported, it produces clean formatting. Because it is plain text and small in size, it is easy to store long-term and unlikely to become corrupted.

**What is Markdown not suited for?**

Markdown is not suited for complex tables (for example, tables that require merged cells or need lists or code inside cells) or highly interactive content (such as animated slides). These needs are better handled by specialized tools or formats.
```